#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j4-0-one-family-one-phone/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Ask the room</0>How do we design for shared phones without compromising each person’s privacy?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j4-0-one-family-one-phone/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Ask the room</0>Is a 4-digit spoken passcode the right balance of security and ease for this family?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j2-found-at-home/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Ask the room</0>Is an “unverified but recorded” vaccine useful to the next clinician — or a risk?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j4-1-full-history-abroad/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Ask the room</0>Should the family be notified every time their child’s record is viewed abroad?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j1-born-abroad/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Ask the room</0>What is the minimum a family should leave hospital with when their baby has no national ID?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j3-made-official/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Ask the room</0>When verification fails, what should the nurse do — and how is it explained to the family?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j2-found-at-home/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Ask the room</0>Who should be allowed to create a health identity for a newborn — and how early?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j3-made-official/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Ask the room</0>Who should own the mapping between countries’ vaccine codes — WHO, each country, or each clinic?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Batch number</0>: Identifies the production batch of a vaccine. Needed for recalls and safety checks."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j1-born-abroad/index.html:0
msgid "<0>birth-clinic-vaccinator-1</0> As a <1>birth clinic vaccinator</1>, I want to print a signed record of each birth dose the family can carry anywhere."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j4-0-one-family-one-phone/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Bounmy’s phone battery dies at the clinic.</0> The link could be printed in advance, and the original paper cards still prove the birth doses."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/walkthrough/J4.0b/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Bounmy</0>: Creates a passcode-protected QR link for <1>Somsak</1>, valid for 14 days."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/walkthrough/J4.0a/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Bounmy</0>: Opens the family wallet: profiles for himself, <1>Khamla</1> and <2>Somsak</2>."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j1-born-abroad/index.html:0
msgid "<0>caregiver-1</0> As a <1>caregiver</1>, I want to have my son's birth doses from abroad recognised at home, so that his care does not start over and nothing is repeated."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j4-0-one-family-one-phone/index.html:0
msgid "<0>caregiver-2</0> As a <1>caregiver</1>, I want to show each family member's records abroad from our one shared phone, with a passcode I can say aloud, so that a doctor abroad can treat us without paper or an app."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j4-0-one-family-one-phone/index.html:0
msgid "<0>caregiver-3</0> As a <1>caregiver</1>, I want to decide who sees my child's record, and for how long, so that the record stays at home and I know who has looked."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/walkthrough/J3b/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Chanthason</0>: Confirms the Taifafeki product equals the birth dose on the Onesa schedule; gives the overdue 6-week vaccines."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/walkthrough/J3a/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Chanthason</0>: Scans the card; the tablet confirms the Taifafeki signature and marks the doses verified."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t7/index.html:0
msgid "<0>CHW app</0> (The health worker's phone): Scan a vaccination card, add the child to the household, and refer them to a clinic. Steps J2a, J2b."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Civil registration and vital statistics (CRVS)</0>: Birth registration can start a child's immunization record."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Client Registry</0>: The Client Registry is the national authoritative source of health-specific person identity. It is the foundational health-sector component that maintains a unique, verifiable identity record for every person who accesses or is eligible to access health services within a jurisdiction."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t7/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Clinic app</0> (The nurse's tablet): Receive the referral, verify the card against the trust list, and plan the next visit. Steps J3a, J3b."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j2-found-at-home/index.html:0
msgid "<0>community-health-worker-1</0> As a <1>community health worker</1>, I want to read a foreign vaccination QR offline and register the child with it, so that the clinic sees what was given before the family arrives."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j2-found-at-home/index.html:0
msgid "<0>community-health-worker-2</0> As a <1>community health worker</1>, I want to refer a child whose foreign record needs checking, so that verification is done by someone who can."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j2-found-at-home/index.html:0
msgid "<0>community-health-worker-3</0> As a <1>community health worker</1>, I want to register a newborn into the household offline, before civil registration, so that no newborn in my village is missed, even with no signal."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Computable Decision Support Engine</0>: The Computable Decision Support Engine is a governed, shared application component that delivers context-appropriate, evidence-based guidance at the point of clinical decision-making by applying computable clinical rules and knowledge artefacts to person-specific health data."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Consent</0>: A person's permission for their data to be used or shared. Rules for minors and dependants differ by country."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Core data set</0>: The elements a country agrees to record for a use case, each mapped to standard codes. Also called a minimum data set."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Digital adaptation kit (DAK)</0>: Software-neutral L2 content: personas, workflows, core data dictionary, decision logic, indicators and requirements."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Digital signature</0>: A cryptographic seal made with the issuer's private key. Verifiers check it with the matching public key."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Digital wallet</0>: An app where a person holds their credentials. A signed paper QR code can play the same role."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Dose number and series</0>: Which dose this is, out of how many in the schedule. Needed to work out what is due next."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/walkthrough/J1/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Dr. Anan</0>: Gives Hep B and BCG birth doses and prints two signed QR vaccine cards."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/walkthrough/J4.1/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Dr. Anan</0>: Scans the QR, enters the passcode <1>Bounmy</1> tells him, and sees all six doses."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Electronic immunization registry (EIR)</0>: Records each person's doses. Often the first working part of a lifelong record."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Expanded Programme on Immunization (EPI)</0>: The national immunization programme."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j2-found-at-home/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Facilitator:</0> Ask who in the room has worked with CHWs. What does “offline” really mean in their context?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j4-0-one-family-one-phone/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Facilitator:</0> Ask: what is inside this QR? (Answer: not the health data — just a pointer and a key.)"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j4-1-full-history-abroad/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Facilitator:</0> Close the loop: the story started and ends in Taifafeki. Ask what changed for each persona since step 1."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j3-made-official/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Facilitator:</0> Emphasize: the Taifafeki record is never overwritten. Both codes live side by side."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j4-0-one-family-one-phone/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Facilitator:</0> Notice Khamla’s mood dips here. Ask the room why — this is the equity tension in the story."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j3-made-official/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Facilitator:</0> Open screen S4 (See what Nurse Chanthason sees) and switch it from Valid card to Tampered card live. The contrast lands better than any explanation."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j1-born-abroad/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Facilitator:</0> Start with Khamla, not the technology. Hold up a paper card: this is the only thing that crosses the border."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j2-found-at-home/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Facilitator:</0> This is the key trust boundary in the story. Pause and make sure everyone sees why the CHW does not verify."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Facility, workforce and product registries</0>: Authoritative lists of health facilities, health workers, and products such as vaccines and their batches."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t7/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Family app</0> (The parent's phone): Hold the family's records and share a child's record as a health link. Steps J4.0a, J4.0b."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Fast Healthcare Interoperability Resources (FHIR)</0>: FHIR is a standard for healthcare data exchange, published by HL7®"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>For:</0> Developers, implementers and digital health architects, working in teams on one app of the journey each"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>For:</0> Ministry of Health policy makers and digital health leads, at tables of one country each"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Global Digital Health Certification Network (GDHCN)</0>: WHO Global Digital Health Certification Network. A trust network so countries can verify each other's health documents. Countries onboard per use case."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/personas/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Goal:</0> Get every vaccine he needs, once, wherever he is."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/personas/anan/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Goal:</0> Give a non-Taifafeki baby proper care, at birth and when he returns."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/personas/khamla-sengmany/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Goal:</0> Have Somsak's care recognized at home, without starting over."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/personas/bounmy-sengmany/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Goal:</0> Keep the whole family's health records in one place he controls."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/personas/vilay/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Goal:</0> Make sure no newborn in her village is missed, even with no signal."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/personas/chanthason/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Goal:</0> Trust foreign records enough to avoid repeating or missing vaccines."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/walkthrough/J3b/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Hand-off:</0> <1>Somsak</1> continues on the Onesa schedule for a year"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/walkthrough/J4.0a/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Hand-off:</0> <1>Somsak</1>’s summary is ready to share"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/walkthrough/J4.0b/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Hand-off:</0> A QR on Dad’s phone + a passcode he can say aloud"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/walkthrough/J4.1/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Hand-off:</0> Journey complete — full circle back to Taifafeki"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/walkthrough/J2b/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Hand-off:</0> Referral to the District Health Center"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/walkthrough/J2a/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Hand-off:</0> The doses, read but not checked, go into the registration"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/walkthrough/J1/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Hand-off:</0> Two paper cards go home with <1>Khamla</1>"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/walkthrough/J3a/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Hand-off:</0> Verified doses, ready to schedule"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Health certificate identifier (HCID)</0>: The unique ID of an issued certificate."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Health information exchange (HIE)</0>: The layer that routes data securely between systems."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j3-made-official/index.html:0
msgid "<0>home-clinic-provider-1</0> As a <1>home clinic provider</1>, I want to know whether a foreign certificate is genuine, and why not when it is not."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j3-made-official/index.html:0
msgid "<0>home-clinic-provider-2</0> As a <1>home clinic provider</1>, I want to see which doses are due once the foreign doses are imported, so that I give only what is missing."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j3-made-official/index.html:0
msgid "<0>home-clinic-provider-3</0> As a <1>home clinic provider</1>, I want to keep the foreign vaccine code and add our schedule code beside it, deciding myself when there is no match, so that the other country's record is never overwritten and the next nurse need not decide again."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>How urgent:</0> Blocks us now · Needed within 12 months · Can wait"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Implementation guide (IG)</0>: A FHIR specification for one use case: profiles, codes and tests. It can be adopted rather than authored."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>International Certificate of Vaccination or Prophylaxis (ICVP)</0>: The \"yellow card\". The digital ICVP is its signed, verifiable form."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>International Patient Summary (IPS)</0>: A standard minimal health summary, including immunizations, readable across borders."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Interoperability</0>: Interoperability is the standards-based capability of heterogeneous information systems to communicate, exchange data, and use the exchanged information to execute functions effectively."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Issuer · holder · verifier</0>: The three roles: who signs the credential, who keeps it, and who checks it."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j1-born-abroad/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J1</0> A baby from Onesa is born in Taifafeki"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/personas/anan/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J1</0> T0 · Birth day · Kesaro Provincial Hospital"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t1/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J1</0>: Patient and Immunization in the hospital record; each dose signed as a DVC (HCERT)."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t3/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J1</0>: The document signer key of Taifafeki (DSC of XXR) signs each DVC as a CWT in COSE."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j2-found-at-home/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J2a</0> A health worker finds the baby — and reads his cards"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/personas/khamla-sengmany/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J2a</0> T0 + 7 weeks · Catchment Village 04"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t2/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J2a</0>: The CHW app decodes the paper cards (read-unverified) and fills the form from them, without checking signatures."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j2-found-at-home/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J2b</0> Registered at home, and referred"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/personas/bounmy-sengmany/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J2b</0> T0 + 7 weeks · Catchment Village 04"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t5/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J2b</0>: A child born abroad and registered at home enters the coverage denominator here."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t7/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J2b</0>: CHW app team: the registration form, the household, the referral."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t4/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J2b</0>: Everything Vilay records stays queued on the phone, for up to 28 days, and syncs when a signal returns."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t2/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J2b</0>: The household registration Questionnaire; answers become Patient, Group (household) and reported Immunization, queued offline."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/personas/chanthason/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J3a</0> T0 + 10 weeks · Lomaru District Health Center"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j3-made-official/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J3a</0> The clinic confirms the cards are genuine"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t7/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J3a</0>: Clinic app team: the verifier and its trust store."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t6/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J3a</0>: Scan, Base45 and zlib decode, COSE signature check against the trust list, then import with provenance."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t3/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J3a</0>: The clinic verifies each card offline against its cached copy of the GDHCN trust list, by kid."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/personas/chanthason/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J3b</0> T0 + 10 weeks · Lomaru District Health Center"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j3-made-official/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J3b</0> Taifafeki vaccines are fitted to the Onesa schedule"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t1/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J3b</0>: ConceptMap from the product codes of Taifafeki to the schedule codes of Onesa; the schedule as a PlanDefinition."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t4/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J3b</0>: The Onesa schedule (PlanDefinition) runs over every dose; at 10 weeks the 6-week doses come out overdue."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t5/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J3b</0>: Verified doses, including those given abroad, count toward coverage indicators."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j4-0-one-family-one-phone/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J4.0a</0> One phone holds the whole family’s records"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/personas/bounmy-sengmany/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J4.0a</0> T0 + 12 months · Lomaru, Onesa"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t7/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J4.0a</0>: Family app team: one phone, one profile and one link per member."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j4-0-one-family-one-phone/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J4.0b</0> Dad creates a link to share at the clinic"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/personas/bounmy-sengmany/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J4.0b</0> T0 + 12 months · Onesa–Taifafeki Friendship Bridge"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t4/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J4.0b</0>: The family's consent is recorded before the portal issues the link; the gateway enforces passcode, expiry and consent on every request."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t1/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J4.0b</0>: The IPS as a FHIR document Bundle assembled from the national record."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t6/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J4.0b</0>: The portal encrypts the IPS and DVCs, publishes a manifest and signs the link as an HCERT."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j4-1-full-history-abroad/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J4.1</0> A doctor in Taifafeki sees the full history"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/personas/anan/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J4.1</0> T0 + 12 months · Kesaro paediatric clinic"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t5/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J4.1</0>: AuditEvents become an access log you can chart."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t4/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J4.1</0>: Each view is logged as an AuditEvent in Onesa, including failed passcode attempts."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t6/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J4.1</0>: The viewer fetches the manifest with an HTTP Message Signature, sends the passcode, and decrypts the documents."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t3/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J4.1</0>: The viewer verifies the VHL's HCERT against the DSC of Onesa (XXU) before it fetches anything."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t7/index.html:0
msgid "<0>J4.1</0>: Viewer app team: open the link, enter the passcode, read the records."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j4-0-one-family-one-phone/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Khamla travels alone with Somsak.</0> Who can access the baby’s record without Bounmy’s phone? Delegated access within a household is still an open design question."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Lifelong Health Record</0>: The Lifelong Health Record (LHR) is one or more governed data repositories, whether physically consolidated or virtually federated, that collectively maintain a longitudinal, person-centred record of an individual's key health information across care settings and over their lifetime."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Logical information model</0>: The agreed structure of the data: elements, types and rules, independent of any software."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>M1</0> From journey to capabilities"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>M2</0> The reference architecture (DPI-H) and where you stand"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>M3</0> Standards, specifications and the core data set"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>M4</0> Trust, credentials and wallets"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>M5</0> Governance, decision rights and the legal basis"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>M6</0> Doing it together"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>M7</0> First move and the investment required"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Personal health record (PHR)</0>: Health information the person can see and control, for example in a wallet or citizen app."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j4-1-full-history-abroad/index.html:0
msgid "<0>poc-provider-1</0> As a <1>poc provider</1>, I want to read a visiting child's summary and vaccinations from a QR the parent shows, so that without installing anything or calling another country."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j4-1-full-history-abroad/index.html:0
msgid "<0>poc-provider-2</0> As a <1>poc provider</1>, I want to know the record I read abroad came from the child's home country and was not altered, so that I can rely on it as I would on my own clinic's record."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Point-of-Service Applications</0>: Point-of-service applications are end-user application components (IT systems or software tools) used by individuals directly engaged in healthcare—such as clinicians, community health workers, and patients—that enable interaction with the broader healthcare ecosystem."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j1-born-abroad/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy point.</0> Babies born abroad can get a verifiable vaccine record before they have the host country’s civil registration or a national ID — and registering the birth at home still matters."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j4-1-full-history-abroad/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy point.</0> Continuity of care across borders: each country keeps its own records, with no international patient registry and no vendor lock-in. What is agreed regionally is the data model and the trust list, not a shared copy of the data."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j4-0-one-family-one-phone/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy point.</0> Data sovereignty: the record stays in Onesa until the family authorizes someone to open it."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j4-0-one-family-one-phone/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy point.</0> Design for shared devices (“One Family, One Phone”) so families with only one phone aren’t left out."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j2-found-at-home/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy point.</0> Keep a clear line between what families report and what has been verified, and don’t grant trust too early."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j3-made-official/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy point.</0> Never overwrite another country’s record: keep the original coding alongside the national one."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j2-found-at-home/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy point.</0> Newborns can be registered at home, offline, before civil registration or a national ID exists."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j3-made-official/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy point.</0> Trust is decentralized: a clinic in Onesa verifies a signature from Taifafeki itself, without contacting Taifafeki."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> Does a dose given abroad count toward your national schedule?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> For a child born abroad, does each touchpoint in your country work, partly work, or break today?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> If your clinics cannot verify a foreign record yet, is that your first move, and who pays for key management year after year?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> If your country cannot issue a signed record yet, is that your first move?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> Is a family wallet a national service, a private app or both, and who approves the apps that may hold a record?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> Is continuity of the record across a border the end point of your use case?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> Is there a national record for a shared link to point to?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> Should a foreign record be verified in each clinic, or by one national service?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> Should neighbouring countries build one vaccine code map together instead of each building their own?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> Should the family or the state decide when a child's record is shared?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> Should the part of the record that crosses borders be profiled once for the region, with national extensions left sovereign?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> Should the trust network be built once for the region and every programme, not for immunization alone?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> What agreement makes every view abroad leave an entry in your home log, and who reads it?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> What is your twelve-month first move, who owns it, and which cost dominates it?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> What legal basis lets a clinician abroad open a record held at home on the family's consent, and who sets how the link is protected?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> What legal basis lets a facility issue a health credential to a child who is not a citizen and has no national ID?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> What must be true before a nurse trusts a vaccination record she did not create?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> What would your country bring to a regional connectathon within twelve months?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> Where does your own journey break first: is there a stage where no national system knows the child exists?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> Which block gives a child their first identifier, and how does a birth abroad enter your registries and your coverage denominator?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> Which block of your national architecture does each of these systems map to, and does it exist today?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> Which child, which record and which border would your country's use case cover?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> Who in your country defines the data element that tells a reported dose from a verified one?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> Who is allowed to verify a foreign credential: a health worker's phone, a clinic, or only a national service?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> Who may create a health identity for a newborn at a home visit, and on whose consent?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> Who may hold and share a child's record, and what does your law say about dependants?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> Who owns your national core data set and the code maps to other countries, and is vaccine code licensing settled?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> Who signs a vaccination record on behalf of your health sector: the hospital, the ministry, or a national trust service?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> Who verifies your citizens' records abroad, and what may that verifier see?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> Who would hold your national trust anchor and accept a foreign signature, and what must be decided before you join the GDHCN?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> Will you adopt the immunization core data set, or design your own national form?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/discuss/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Policy.</0> Will you adopt the IPS and the VHL specification as they are, and author only national extensions?"
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j4-0-one-family-one-phone/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Precondition, as in J1:</0> Country B's DSC, under Country B's CSCA, is already shared with the GDHCN, the Trust Anchor. That is what lets the clinic in Taifafeki verify the link in J4.1."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j4-1-full-history-abroad/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Precondition, as in J3: the DID documents are already loaded.</0> The clinic viewer's trust store is a cached copy of the GDHCN trust list, including Country B's DSC DID document (STT-TRU-001, STT-TRU-002, STT-TRU-005). The clinic refreshes it nightly or hourly, against about weekly at the offline J3 clinic. It does not need to be online to verify: verifying reads the cache and never fetches the list. A DSC published after the last refresh fails the trust-list check (STT-VER-006), naming that reason."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j3-made-official/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Precondition: the DID documents are already loaded.</0> Loading them is not a step of this visit. The clinic may be offline all day, so the EHR fetches nothing during it: its trust store holds the GDHCN DEV trust list as it was last refreshed, including XXR's DSC DID document (STT-TRU-001, STT-TRU-002, STT-TRU-005). A clinic with no connection of its own refreshes it about weekly, when the CHW visits the base clinic or district health office, where Country B retrieves the list the GDHCN trust anchor distributes. A DSC published after that refresh is not in the clinic's copy, so its DVC fails the trust-list check (STT-VER-006) until the next refresh."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/j1-born-abroad/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Precondition: the issuer's DSC is on the trust list.</0> XXR's document signer certificate (DSC), issued under XXR's Country Signing CA (CSCA), was shared with the GDHCN, the Trust Anchor, before any DVC is signed; the GDHCN publishes it as a DID document. Sharing it is not a step of issuing. A DVC signed with a key whose DSC was never shared fails every receiver's trust-list check (STT-VER-006)."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Procurement conditions</0>: Requirements written into tenders, such as conformance to the national IG, that steer what suppliers build."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Profile</0>: A FHIR resource tailored to a use case, for example by making some fields required."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/index.html:0
msgid "<0>Public key infrastructure (PKI)</0>: The keys, certificates and rules that make digital signatures trustworthy."
msgstr ""

